# Everything the backend image must not carry.
#
# Two of these are correctness issues rather than size ones:
#   venv/          holds Windows binaries and a Python 3.14 site-packages tree;
#                  copied into a Linux 3.12 image it would shadow the container's
#                  own installs with libraries that cannot load.
#   .env           contains a real API key. It reaches the container through
#                  compose's `environment:` block at RUN time, which keeps it out
#                  of the image layers -- an ENV baked into an image is readable
#                  by anyone who can pull it.

venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

.env

.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore

frontend/
node_modules/

samples/
README.md
docker-compose.yml

.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
